      "id": "ALE-416",
      "uuid": "fd28be76-4890-46f7-b1fa-652da1f43251",
      "title": "Inventory: give the Items page a tested controller",
      "description": "> **Triage:** ready-for-agent. From the `apps/web` architecture review, grilled to agreement on 12 Oct 2026.\n\n## Problem Statement\n\n`routes/dashboard/inventory/items/[[itemId]]/+page.svelte` is 1,673 lines and acts as its own controller. Its 393-line script holds 27 `$state`, 2 `$effect`, 9 `createQuery`, 4 TanStack mutations and 6 remote forms:\n\n* **Two command paths.** Archive (which has a reason field), Restore and Delete go through TanStack; create, update, move, change category and start/end maintenance go through remote forms.\n* **Property values three times over.** Create, edit and change-category each keep their own value map, encoded as JSON in hidden inputs, with `JSON.stringify` dirty checks (L201, L211). `displayValue` renders booleans as \"true\"/\"false\" (`String(value.boolean)`) while the edit form says Yes/No: a backend value leaking into copy.\n* **Schemas inline.** The three inventory `data.remote.ts` files define 11 `v.object` schemas, against the \"one schema per form in `lib/schemas/`\" rule.\n* **Local list state.** Search, filters and cursor live in local `$state`, not the URL.\n* **No tests.** Items, Categories and Containers together are 3,635 lines of Svelte without one.\n\n## Solution\n\n* **Controller.** Add `routes/dashboard/inventory/items/[[itemId]]/item-workbench.svelte.ts`, a runes controller in the shape of `routes/dashboard/inventory/loans/loan-queue-board.svelte.ts`. It owns:\n  * the list request, URL-backed through `createCursorTableUrl` (search, archived, availability from <issue id=\"a10ccedb-a456-4c4a-951d-fb35982a1e88\" label=\"ALE-415\" href=\"https://linear.app/alessandrojcm/issue/ALE-415/inventory-the-items-availability-filter-only-searches-the-current-page\" />, cursor; replace for search/filters, push for cursor paging);\n  * routed selection (`[[itemId]]`, `new`, the `?slug=` deep link);\n  * the drafts and their dirty state;\n  * every command's outcome (toast, refresh, success flash).\n    The page only renders and binds.\n* **One command path.** Every Item command (create, update, move, change category, start/end maintenance, archive with reason, restore, delete) is a remote form through `inventoryCommand` with `inventoryManageOptions()`. Delete returns to the list on success.\n* **Schemas.** Move them to `lib/schemas/inventoryItem.ts`: one per form, built from the field validators, output `satisfies` the generated request body, and the same object is passed to `.preflight(schema)`.\n* **Property values.** Add `lib/inventory/property-values.ts`, a pure module with unit tests owning:\n  * one draft-map type and its conversion from an item (replaces `itemValues`);\n  * the hidden-field encoding (JSON stays);\n  * the dirty comparison;\n  * display formatting (Yes/No for booleans, option labels, decimals) for the list rows (replaces `displayValue`).\n    The member equipment views can use it too.\n\n## Tests\n\n* `item-workbench.svelte.browser.test.ts`: list/URL state, selection, each command's success and refusal, dirty state.\n* `lib/inventory/property-values.test.ts`.\n\n## Next (not this ticket)\n\nCategories (`categories/[[categoryId]]/+page.svelte`, 1,245 lines, 18 `$state`) and Containers (`containers/+page.svelte`, 717 lines) follow the same pattern once this one lands. Create their tickets then, from what this ticket settles.\n\n## Constraints\n\n* **Copy.** Staff- and person-facing copy uses the vocabulary in `AGENTS.md` (Beginners' Workshops: \"Manage\", \"workshop place\", \"offer round\", \"workshop credit\", \"payment deadline\", \"attendance confirmed\"; inventory: quartermaster / item / gear / code). It never shows a domain identifier or enum value (\"Intake\", \"Carried Fee\", \"operator\", \"slug\", snake_case values). Domain identifiers, enums and API field names stay unchanged.\n* **Contracts are spec-first.** `apps/phoenix/priv/api/openapi.yaml` → Phoenix → `mise run api-gen` (idempotent: only `skip` lines), with the slice's client parity test.\n* **Replace tests, don't layer them.** New tests sit at the new interface; superseded tests are deleted. Runes controllers are tested as `*.svelte.browser.test.ts` with injected requests (the documented test-seam exception); no `vi.mock`.\n* **Green before done.** `mise run ci`, `mise run phx-test` and `mise run phx-precommit` (Reach included) where Phoenix changes.\n* Record in `AGENTS.md` / `docs/agents/where-to-look.md` only what a future agent would otherwise get wrong.",
