      "id": "ALE-143",
      "uuid": "6de86e3b-3fbc-4ec9-8ed5-a14a57bb88a1",
      "title": "Recover Notification realtime across connection and session changes",
      "description": "## Parent\n\nALE-140\n\n## What to build\n\nKeep Notification state convergent as Phoenix reconnects and Supabase sessions change. Every connected client repairs missed signals through the authoritative HTTP API, refreshed tokens replace old connections, and sign-out or component teardown removes authenticated realtime state.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Successful initial joins and rejoins invalidate the existing Notifications infinite-query key.\n- [ ] Events missed while disconnected are recovered through API refetch rather than replay or event payload data.\n- [ ] Duplicate signals and repeated invalidations do not duplicate Notifications in the interface.\n- [ ] `TOKEN_REFRESHED` leaves and disconnects the old channel/socket and creates a new connection with the refreshed access token.\n- [ ] `SIGNED_OUT` and component cleanup remove authentication listeners, leave the channel, and disconnect the socket.\n- [ ] Connection, join, authentication, and reconnect failures remain unobtrusive and do not disable Notification queries or mutations.\n- [ ] Focused component tests cover join/rejoin recovery, token rotation, teardown, and preserved HTTP behavior after realtime failures.\n\n## Blocked by\n\n* ALE-142",
